    {
     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"ml\" data-a=\"200\">200 ml</span>",
     "name_html": "Water (rice)"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Drain the tuna well. Mix with the mayonnaise and soy sauce, then add the sriracha a little at a time and taste.</li><li>Use <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tsp\" data-a=\"1\" data-b=\"2\" data-s=\"0\">1–2 tsp</span> in each onigiri. Keep any extra filling chilled; do not overfill the rice.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-2",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Prepare the spicy tuna-mayo",
    "diagram": null,
    "diagram_title": "Diagram",
    "how": [],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": null,
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 2,
   "part": "Filling",
   "part_id": "part-filling",
   "time": "~3 min",
   "time_html": "<span>~3 min</span>",
   "title": "Prepare the spicy tuna-mayo",
   "uses_rows": [
    {
     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"mass\" data-u=\"g\" data-a=\"50\">50 g</span>",
     "name_html": "Canned tuna, drained"
    },
    {
     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tbsp\" data-a=\"1\">1 tbsp</span>",
     "name_html": "Japanese mayo (Kewpie)"
    },
    {
     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tsp\" data-a=\"0.5\">½ tsp</span>",
     "name_html": "Soy sauce (tuna-mayo)"
    },
    {
     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tsp\" data-a=\"0.5\" data-b=\"1\">½–1 tsp</span>",
     "name_html": "Sriracha"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Let the rice cool just until you can hold it — it must still be warm to stick.</li><li>Wet both palms with a little water.</li><li>Dip 2–3 fingers in kosher salt and rub it over both palms (table salt: half as much).</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-3",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Wet and salt your hands",
    "diagram": null,
    "diagram_title": "Diagram",
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Wet both palms, then dip 2–3 fingers in kosher salt…",
      "src": "illustrations/kimchi-cheese-onigiri/3-how1.webp?v=522ee31760"
     },
     {
      "caption": "…and rub the salt over both palms.",
      "src": "illustrations/kimchi-cheese-onigiri/3-how2.webp?v=8ecc676131"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/kimchi-cheese-onigiri/3.webp?v=6e4c345ccc",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 3,
   "part": "Shape by hand",
   "part_id": "part-shape-by-hand",
   "time": "~5 min",
   "time_html": "<span>~5 min</span>",
   "title": "Wet and salt your hands",
   "uses_rows": [
    {
     "amount_html": "a little for each onigiri",
     "name_html": "Kosher salt (for your hands)"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Scoop ~<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"mass\" data-u=\"g\" data-a=\"50\" data-s=\"0\">50 g</span> warm rice onto your LEFT palm — the left hand always stays underneath.</li><li>Press a small well in the middle and put in <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tsp\" data-a=\"1\" data-b=\"2\" data-s=\"0\">1–2 tsp</span> of one filling.</li><li>Cover with another ~<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"mass\" data-u=\"g\" data-a=\"50\" data-s=\"0\">50 g</span> of rice and press it gently round the filling into a ball.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-4",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Rice, filling, close",
    "diagram": null,
    "diagram_title": "Diagram",
    "how": [],
    "illustration": "illustrations/kimchi-cheese-onigiri/4.webp?v=a2447717ab",
    "photo": null,
    "result": null,
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 4,
   "part": "Shape by hand",
   "part_id": "part-shape-by-hand",
   "time": "1 min each",
   "time_html": "<span>1 min each</span>",
   "title": "Rice, filling, close",
   "uses_rows": []
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>RIGHT hand on top, fingers together and bent into a roof — it makes the corner.</li><li>LEFT hand underneath in a “C” — fingers and heel gently flatten the two sides.</li><li>Press lightly, then roll the corner you just made <b>towards you</b> — a third of a turn.</li><li>Three corners, then 2–3 more rounds. Lay it on each face and press once to flatten.</li><li>Firm enough to hold together, but airy inside — don’t squeeze.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-5",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Press the triangle",
    "diagram": null,
    "diagram_title": "Diagram",
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Right hand on top, fingers together and bent like a roof; left hand underneath in a “C”, pressing the sides.",
      "src": "illustrations/kimchi-cheese-onigiri/5-how1.webp?v=f09f821ccb"
     },
     {
      "caption": "Press lightly, then roll the corner you just made towards you — a third of a turn — and press again.",
      "src": "illustrations/kimchi-cheese-onigiri/5-how2.webp?v=5c94e8c191"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/kimchi-cheese-onigiri/5.webp?v=bddbbe9acb",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 5,
   "part": "Shape by hand",
   "part_id": "part-shape-by-hand",
   "time": "~1 min each",
   "time_html": "<span>~1 min each</span>",
   "title": "Press the triangle",
   "uses_rows": []
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Wrap a third of a nori sheet round the bottom of each onigiri just before eating for crisp nori.</li><li>Or coat the faces in furikake with damp fingers. Serve freshly made.</li><li>The cut section shows this filling enclosed in rice. Cutting one open is optional.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
